# A full-length thread follows its face (an extension): the side of an
# extruded circle, picked on the model, is threaded over its whole
# length; the extrusion's depth is then held and typed as 100, and the
# thread, not edited, is 100 long with it; typed as 1, too short for a
# thread, the thread keeps its length and reports why.
